# No dishwasher / washing machine (HARD — copy law)

**Owner letters 2026-08-21 and 2026-08-26.** Care is hand wash only. Naming a dishwasher or washing machine — even to say “don’t” — puts the idea in the customer’s head.

## Banned — never write these

dishwasher · washing machine · machine wash · machine washing · machine dryer · “no machine washing” · “never machine wash” · “some customers run theirs through the dishwasher” · “dry in seconds”

## Say instead — the only sanctioned wording (P-005)

**“Hand wash with warm soapy water. That's it.”**

```
✅ "Hand wash with warm soapy water. That's it."
❌ "Warm soapy water, rinse, air dry. No machine washing."
❌ "Dry in seconds."
❌ "Some customers use the dishwasher."
```

